 bit  less tempted to just smash your skin  every night with the strongest actives  possible  because i know that feeling so the first  product that i picked for the box that i  knew i had to include  is the claire's soft airy uv essence  this is a sunscreen that i've had in my  holy grails list for a really long time  i'm sure you all already have a  sunscreen in your routine but  we have to use a lot of sunscreen so  it's a product you'll probably be able  to use up  this is a light water-based sunscreen  and it has a really nice texture  it's also alcohol-free alcohol isn't  really bad for your skin but if it's  irritated it can sting a little bit  it's a chemical sunscreen that uses some  of the newer photostable filters  including one of my favorites  juvenile a plus it has a light scent no  white cast  and it's rated spf 50 plus and pa plus  plus plus  plus which is the highest rating you can  get for korean sunscreen  as well as protecting your skin from uv  there's also some skincare ingredients  in it there's sea buckthorn oil which  has antioxidants to protect your skin  from free radicals  there's also alan tone beta glucan and  niacinamide which are all really good at  soothing skin  it works really well for everyday use  under makeup and it also works really  well over makeup so you can reapply it  using a cushion  it's actually the sunscreen that i used  in my demonstration  for how to reapply sunscreen over makeup  the next product is buy wishtrend's  mandelic acid 5  skin prep water if you're a skincare  nerd you probably already have an alpha  hydroxy acid exfoliant in your routine  most of the time when you have aha  exfoliants you have  lactic acid and glycolic acid mandelic  acid is a bit harder to find  it's a really gentle alpha hydroxy acid  it's larger so it  has a bit of a harder time getting into  your skin and so it's less likely to  cause irritation  it's also got a really low concentration  of five percent so this is really good  to use when your skin is irritated but  you still want to exfoliate a little bit  it also has a bunch of soothing  ingredients in it we have  beta-glucan panthenol licorice fruit and  centella extracts  so this is really good if your skin  needs a little bit of a break but not  that much of a break then we have the  claire's midnight blue calming cream  this is a really popular korean beauty  product it's  really amazing at soothing irritation so  it's really good if you've got chapped  skin or if you've gone too hard on  actives  it has this really pretty blue color  which comes from the active gua  azulene this is a natural product that  comes from chamomile and it's really  good at calming down skin  it's also got cintella extract which is  great at healing your skin  and amazingly it doesn't have  niacinamide it's getting really hard to  find products that don't have  niacinamide in them  and so if you want to give your skin a  break from niacinamide or if your skin  doesn't like niacinamide that much  this is a really nice product to use  there's lots of humectant moisturizers  in this  these are really good at holding water  to your skin especially if your skin's  dehydrated they're really great so  glycerin and hyaluronic acid  there's also some moisturizing oils like  jojoba oil argan oil and shea butter  the texture of this is slightly thicker  than a gel  but i didn't find it oily or greasy it  also has no noticeable scent  then we have the buy wishtrend quad  active boosting essence  this is a really lightweight soothing  toner usually i'm a bit hesitant with  plant extracts because they can be  irritating  but when a product purposely chooses  soothing calming plant extracts that's  not really a problem  using plant extracts is a really good  way of getting a huge range of  antioxidants into a product and so  having this variety of antioxidants  means that it's more likely to work  and the antioxidants can keep each other  activated inside the product so they  